<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea 3-yr yields end lower on scanty new issues.</title>
<headline>S.Korea 3-yr yields end lower on scanty new issues.</headline>
<text>
<p>Yields on three-year corporate bonds closed lower on Tuesday due to relatively smaller new issues and continued buying interest from institutions, brokers said.</p>
<p>Three-month CD yields fell due to an improvement in short-term liquidity. Overnight call remained unchanged.</p>
<p>* 3-yr corporates end at 12.60 pct from Monday's 12.67</p>
<p>* 3-mth CDs close at 12.40 pct from 12.45</p>
<p>* Overnight call average unchanged at 12.80 pct</p>
</text>
